  "worked_solution": "This is a two-step random process: first, a level difficulty is selected uniformly from the integers $1$ through $500,$ and then a treasure chest is placed uniformly in one of the zones numbered $1$ through $d,$ where $d$ is the selected difficulty.\n\n- Let $Y$ be the difficulty level of the chosen level. Since the difficulty is chosen uniformly from $1$ to $500,$ we have $Y∼U\\{1,2,…,500\\}.$\n\n- Let $X$ be the number of the zone where the chest is placed, which is chosen uniformly from $1$ to $Y.$\n\nWe are asked to compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Since $X$ depends on $Y,$ we apply the tower property:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\text{E}[\\text{E}[X∣Y]]\n$$\n\nGiven $Y=d,$ the zone is selected uniformly from $1$ to $d.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X∣Y=d]=\\frac{d+1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\text{E}[\\frac{Y+1}{2}].\n$$\n\nNow, we apply the linearity of expectation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\text{E}[Y+1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (\\text{E}[Y]+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Y$ is uniformly distributed on $\\{1,2,…,500\\},$ we compute\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{1+500}{2}=250.5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (250.5+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 251.5 \\\\  & =125.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
